---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Editorial policy" description="How Toolwise AI researches, writes, reviews and updates its articles.">
  <Prose title="Editorial policy" lede="How we research, write, review and update what we publish.">
    <h2>Our standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every article must answer a distinct, real reader need. We avoid near-duplicate pages.</li>
      <li>Factual claims about products — features, limits, pricing, privacy terms — are checked against official vendor sources.</li>
      <li>Prices and plan details carry a “checked on” date, because they change often.</li>
      <li>We never fabricate hands-on testing, results, screenshots, quotes or author credentials.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How AI is used</h2>
    <p>
      We write about AI tools and we use them in our own process — for example to help outline, summarize research or
      suggest edits. AI output is treated as a draft, never as a source. A person verifies the facts, removes
      unsupported claims and decides whether an article is useful enough to publish.
    </p>
    <h2>Review before publication</h2>
    <p>
      Each article goes through a human review before it is published. Articles that have not passed review are kept
      as drafts and are not published on the site.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
    <p>
      If we get something wrong, we fix it and note the update date on the article. If you spot an error, please
      <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      Recommendations are based on usefulness to readers. Affiliate relationships do not determine which products we
      cover or how we rank them. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
